      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Suren,\n\nIn `arch/arm64/include/asm/pgtable-hwdef.h`, PMD_SHIFT, PUD_SHIFT, and PTRS_PER_PMD are defined directly in terms of PAGE_SHIFT so making PAGE_SHIFT dynamic automatically changes their values.\n\nIn `include/linux/pgtable.h` is `pmd_index()`, `pud_index()`, and `pmd_offset()` as static inline functions compiled earlier in the file with static 16KB shifts (and aliases by macors `#define pmd_index pmd_index`).\n\n#undef and redefining them here as function like macros shadows those static inline functions, forcing subsequent callers in this translation unit to evaluate using the new dynamic shifts instead.",
      "parentUuid": "6bbccabc_ba7b92f2",
